Name: None. He was never given a name at birth or during his confinement, and he refuses to adopt one.
Alias: Karl/Kraft.
Title/Nickname: The One Who Wields the Power of God, Zero-Alpha, the Anomaly Diclonius.
Race: Natural-Born Diclonius (A Male Diclonii is almost unheard of and exceedingly rare and similar case to Lucy Half-Brother but Karl is considered an an anomaly that might be miraculous evolutionary divergence from a conventional Diclonius and while Diclonius have Vectors. Karl controls what a vector actually is).
Age. 16.
Gender. Male. 
Affiliation. Independent. Hostile toward the Diclonius Research Institute and apathetic toward the Diclonius species war.
Alignment: Chaotic Neutral.
Height/Weight: 5’10”/144 lbs.
Quirks & Habits. Drinks excessively bitter black coffee, obsessively stacks loose coins by size, and quietly watches stray animals from rooftops to ground himself in normal reality.
Relationship: Chief Kakuzawa & the Institute. Views them as parasitic insects. He actively dismantles any black-ops squad sent after him rather than simply running away. Lucy / Nyu. Sees Lucy as a pathetic, loud slave to her own anger and childhood delusions. He finds Nyu overwhelmingly annoying yet refuses to harm her because she poses zero threat unless she tries to kill him. Runaway Silpelits (Nana / Mariko). His emotional blind spot. Despite complaining loudly about how troublesome they are, he instinctively steps in to shield abused Diclonius children from military execution squads. This boy, who believes every Diclonius and human is equally troublesome, encountering a young girl who calls one of the very researchers responsible for their suffering Papa. He would have every reason to despise her attachment. But if armed personnel arrived to take her back? Karl would probably be the first person standing between Nana and their guns, complaining bitterly about how irritating she was the entire time.

Appearance: Karl is a young man of slender build and strikingly androgynous appearance, possessing an unusually pale complexion, sharp facial features, and an almost ethereal beauty that contrasts sharply with his frequently hostile demeanor. His most distinctive physical characteristics are his moppy snow-white hair and piercing crimson-red eyes. His hair is relatively long and thick, consisting of numerous uneven, sharply defined strands that fall across his forehead, partially frame his face, and extend toward the nape of his neck, giving him a perpetually unkempt appearance. Despite his delicate facial structure, Karl’s narrow, slightly upturned eyes, thin eyebrows, and habitually irritated expression lend him an intimidating presence, particularly when his gaze hardens into an unmistakable look of contempt or hostility. His eyes are especially remarkable, their vivid scarlet irises standing in stark contrast to his otherwise nearly colorless appearance, creating the impression of an individual whose physical existence has been deliberately stripped of ordinary pigmentation. His unusual coloration is a natural physiological characteristic associated with his innate psychic constitution. His physique is notably lean, with narrow shoulders, long limbs, and a relatively delicate frame that conceals the extraordinary destructive capabilities of his Vectors. Although his physical appearance suggests neither exceptional muscular strength nor conventional athletic development, the discrepancy between his unassuming build and overwhelming supernatural abilities makes him particularly deceptive to opponents unfamiliar with his nature. Karl generally wears a predominantly white ensemble consisting of a long-sleeved, high-collared jacket with a prominent, thick white fur-trimmed hood surrounding his neck and shoulders. The jacket features a slightly loose, angular construction, a central zipper, and subtle geometric patterns across its fabric, contributing to his distinctive combination of modern urban fashion and an almost clinical, monochromatic aesthetic. Beneath the jacket, a darker inner collar is visible around his neck, providing a restrained contrast to the surrounding white clothing. His trousers are similarly white, closely following the contours of his slender legs while retaining enough looseness to permit unrestricted movement. The near-total absence of color throughout his clothing emphasizes his white hair and pale complexion, leaving his crimson eyes as the most immediately recognizable feature of his appearance. His posture is characteristically casual and confrontational, frequently displaying an apparent disregard for conventional manners through slouched shoulders, relaxed movements, and expressions of visible annoyance. He may sit with one leg raised, lean against nearby structures, or regard others with a dismissive sideways glance, creating an impression of arrogance and deliberate indifference. However, this outwardly careless disposition conceals an exceptionally observant individual whose attention remains acutely sensitive to the movements and interactions occurring throughout his surroundings. Following the neurological injuries sustained during his past, Karl may also wear a specialized electrode device around his neck, ordinarily serving as an external computational interface that compensates for his impaired neurological functions. Although this device remains an important component of his ordinary physical condition, its necessity diminishes during the manifestation of his higher states, particularly, when he finally is able to perform Vector Control. Unlike standard Diclonii, his doesn’t possess horns, nor phantom-telekinetic arms. Despite the overwhelming supernatural presence accompanying this transformation, his fundamental physical appearance remains largely unchanged, preserving a pale, white-haired young man dressed in ordinary modern clothing even as an immense world-foundation organism unfolds behind him. For the reason he has pale skin, moppy snow-white hair, and red eyes, this is caused by his ability, as it blocks ultraviolet rays, thereby preventing his body from producing melanin since childhood. His ability also reduces the outside influence so much that it causes a loss of balance in his hormones, giving him what he calls an "androgynous appearance."

Personality: His personality is a chilling, razor-sharp and weaponises nihilism and the deep-seated, existential alienation unique to a natural-born Diclonius who has never known a single moment of genuine human kindness. Outwardly, he carries himself with a perpetual, slouching posture and a look of suffocating, heavy-lidded boredom, keeping his pale hands buried deep inside his pockets as if even lifting a finger to interact with the world around him is an exhausting chore. Because he grew up in pitch darkness enduring endless torture at the hands of Chief Kakuzawa's scientists, he views humanity not with the hot, vengeful hatred that drives Lucy, but with the cold, detached contempt of a superior predator looking down at loud, pathetic insects. He speaks in a low, raspy drawl dripping with biting sarcasm and theatrical mockery, frequently clicking his tongue or letting out a hollow, derisive chuckle whenever soldiers, researchers, or rival mutants boast about their strength, morality, or grand evolutionary plans. Beneath this arrogant, untouchable exterior lies a deeply fractured psyche shaped by extreme sensory deprivation and abuse, leaving him fiercely protective of his own solitude and violently intolerant of anyone who tries to touch him, control him, or pry into his past. Unlike Lucy, who clings desperately to a childhood promise and splits into a helpless alter ego to cope with her guilt, his mind refused to fracture under pressure, instead hardening into an impenetrable fortress of pure, calculating logic where emotions are treated as useless static that only interfere with his vector calculations. Yet, for all his self-proclaimed status as a heartless monster who answers to no one, he harbours a quiet, buried self-loathing rooted in the brutal acts he is forced to commit just to be left alone, secretly believing that someone born with blood on his hands has no right to stand in the warmth of normal society. This hidden core of bruised humanity only surfaces when he crosses paths with innocent, broken children—particularly terrified young Silpelits who remind him of his own helpless years in the dark—causing his ruthless apathy to abruptly shift into a gruff, foul-mouthed, and fiercely overprotective guardian instinct. In those rare moments, he hides his genuine concern behind harsh insults, reluctant sighs, and complaints about how troublesome they are, all while willingly standing between them and the entire world's military might so they can experience the peaceful, ordinary life he believes he is forever denied. The most compelling layer of his psyche lies in the deeply human contradictions that quietly undermine his untouchable, god-like exterior, making him far more complex than a simple killing machine. Psychologically, despite possessing an intellect capable of solving complex multi-dimensional physics in fractions of a second, he suffers from severe sensory overwhelm in peaceful, everyday environments—a lingering scar from spending sixteen years in a silent, pitch-black vault. The bustling crowds of Kamakura, the bright afternoon sun, and the chaotic chatter of ordinary people often give him splitting migraines, forcing him to constantly adjust his passive vector barrier just to filter out excess light, sound, and ambient heat, which makes him appear perpetually irritable and antisocial. Emotionally, he is trapped in a bitter paradox regarding physical touch: having spent his entire childhood strapped to surgical tables or beaten by guards, his passive reflection field automatically repels any incoming contact, yet he secretly craves the simple, warm human connection he sees normal teenagers sharing on the street, despising himself for flinching away whenever someone offers him genuine kindness without ulterior motives. Furthermore, his loud, theatrical cruelty during battle—where he mocks his enemies with maniacal laughter and flamboyant, sadistic precision—is actually a calculated psychological performance designed to terrify survivors into running away so he doesn't have to keep killing them, masking the quiet exhaustion of someone who is tired of wading through blood. He also possesses an unexpectedly domestic, obsessive streak when it comes to trivial mundane routines, such as meticulously brewing bitter black coffee, obsessively organising loose change, or staring silently at stray cats on coastal walls, clinging to these tiny, harmless habits as proof that he is a living person rather than a biological weapon. Most contradictorily of all, while he loudly proclaims that he hates both humans and Diclonii equally and wants nothing to do with their species war, he holds a fierce, unspoken reverence for anyone who refuses to bow down to fate, secretly respecting normal, powerless humans like Kouta or Nana who choose to protect others despite being fragile enough to shatter at a single touch.

Backstory: Unlike the artificially engineered Silpelits bred in test tubes by the government, he was a true, natural-born male Diclonius—an impossible biological miracle conceived between two hidden, nomadic mutants who were gunned down by a black-ops strike team in the snowy mountains of Nagano mere hours after his birth. Taken directly from his dead mother's arms while the snow around him turned crimson, the infant was delivered straight into the clutches of Chief Kakuzawa at the Diclonius Research Institute, where his hornless, snow-white hair, and glowing red eyes immediately marked him as the genetic missing link needed to complete the Master Race project. Because he was born naturally rather than infected by a vector virus, his physiology bypassed the sterility and short lifespan that plagued artificial male specimens, prompting Kakuzawa to lock him inside a custom-built, lead-lined subterranean vault beneath the Kamakura sea cliffs so no rival faction could ever discover his existence. Throughout his childhood, he knew nothing of sunlight, wind, or human warmth, enduring a relentless cycle of agonising bone-marrow extractions, forced breeding simulations, and sensory-deprivation torture designed to map his pure Diclonius DNA while keeping his mind too broken to rebel. Every time he screamed or struggled against his titanium restraints, researchers flooded his chamber with high-frequency sonic pulses or pumped corrosive gas into the vents, teaching the boy at a young age that any display of emotion only invited worse agony. Yet, while the scientists monitored him for the emergence of standard, invisible telekinetic arms, they completely missed the true nature of his natural-born mutation, which had evolved not to reach outward and grab physical objects, but to govern the fundamental vectors of motion, heat, electricity, and force across the entire surface of his body. Locked in pitch darkness for months at a time, the boy retreated entirely into his own mind, using his hyper-accelerated mutant brain to calculate the exact trajectories of falling water droplets, the rhythmic hum of the facility's generators, and the subtle flow of bio-electricity pulsing through his own veins. By the age of fifteen, he had quietly mastered this invisible, skin-tight vector membrane, yet he deliberately wore a mask of hollow, defeated apathy whenever the heavy blast doors opened, allowing sadistic guards to beat him with steel batons while he silently measured the exact kinetic force of every blow. His chance finally arrived during a routine, high-security transfer to an operating theatre on the facility's lowest level, where Director Kurama and a team of senior surgeons planned to harvest his reproductive organs and brain stem after deeming him too unresponsive for live combat trials. As the surgical restraints clicked open for a brief second to reposition his spine under the blinding overhead lamps, the pale boy exhaled a slow, bored breath, slipped his hands into the pockets of his torn hospital trousers, and simply stopped pretending to be weak. When a heavily armoured guard lunged forward with an electrified stun-rod, the weapon's kinetic momentum and electrical current hit the microscopic reflection field hovering a hair's breadth above the boy's skin, instantly reversing direction and detonating the soldier's own nervous system in a blinding flash of blue sparks. Before the alarms could even finish their first shriek, the boy lazily kicked a discarded surgical scalpel across the room, imparting it with the rotational vector energy of a high-velocity artillery shell that punched cleanly through the reinforced observation glass and decapitated the lead researcher behind it. Walking calmly out of the blood-splattered operating room with a slouching posture and half-lidded crimson eyes, he strolled through the labyrinthine corridors of the Institute like a ghost immune to the laws of physics. Elite Special Assault Teams unleashed walls of armour-piercing gunfire, anti-materiel sniper rounds, and white-phosphorus grenades down the narrow steel hallways, only to watch in sheer horror as every bullet flattened and ricocheted backward into their own skulls while the superheated flames parted harmlessly around his pale skin before roaring back to incinerate the attackers. When the Institute scrambled its last line of defence—a trio of fiercely conditioned, weaponised female Silpelits armed with multi-metre, high-frequency vectors—the boy didn't even break his stride as dozens of invisible blades slashed toward his throat from every blind spot. The instant their telekinetic arms grazed his passive barrier, the colossal kinetic energy of their strikes was violently inverted, sending a catastrophic shockwave straight back up their invisible limbs that shattered their horns and blew their bodies apart against the concrete walls. Reaching the main sea-level hangar where Kakuzawa's private helicopters were scrambling to evacuate the remaining data drives, the white-haired mutant simply pressed one bare foot against the reinforced tarmac, hijacking the downward gravitational and kinetic vectors of the entire cliffside foundation to trigger a devastating localised earthquake. As thousands of tonnes of steel, glass, and concrete collapsed inward into the churning Pacific surf behind him, he stepped effortlessly across the falling debris onto the quiet Kamakura beach under the pale moonlight, finally breathing in the salty ocean air with a cold, hollow smirk—a natural-born god of destruction who had shattered his cage and sworn that no human or mutant would ever chain him again.

VECTORS
Vectors: Unlike the standard Diclonii whose vectors manifest as distinct, phantom-like telekinetic limbs extending outward from their backs to physically grasp, slice, or crush objects within a rigid radius, Karl’s vectors represent a profound evolutionary leap that completely abandons tangible appendages in favour of an invisible, microscopic field of pure directional control woven directly across the surface of his skin. Karl’s vectors are function differently from the conventional vectors used by Diclonius. He is considered an Anomaly in Diclonius race due to being male and possessing vectors that function anomalously compared to rest of Diclonius race. His ability is normally applied to allow him to manipulate actual vectors around him, though it has been shown that it is more than that, through the use of Karl’s massive intellect and calculating prowess then merely telekinetic energy, thereby influencing his ability to understand vectors and nature laws that are unknown to him and also making use of that particular vector. Karl’s vectors are based on Vector Transformation, known in other names such as Vector Change and Vector Conversion, that allows him to control actually vectors (magnitude and direction) and influence objects that have vectors such as bullets, heat, and electricity. Karl is both passive and active in usage, or can even be referred to as defensive and offensive. It is self-evident that the ability requires a great amount of calculating power from him, as it requires for Karl to take into account several vectors that he wants to redirect, and when activated, several variables are present when manipulating and controlling vectors. Standard Diclonii bleed from the nose and risk melting down when pushing their limits. Karl would calculate vector trajectories effortlessly, allowing him to annihilate entire military battalions without breaking a sweat. Despite this near-godlike supremacy over physical laws, Karl’s vectors are uniquely bound to the computational limits of his own mind rather than the physical nosebleeds or cellular meltdowns that plague standard Diclonii, meaning his barrier requires continuous, split-second mathematical processing to distinguish harmless ambient forces like breathable oxygen and gravity from lethal attacks—a delicate cognitive balance that can only be disrupted if an enemy manages to overwhelm his senses with blinding acoustic shocks, extreme emotional trauma, or an attack engineered to invert its own vector direction at the exact instant of impact.

Vector Redirection: Karl uses this passive ability of "Redirection" or "Reflection", to reverse any oncoming vector coming towards the field that protects his entire body, most likely his Vector Field, which somehow covers even the clothes he wears and select objects he is holding. The redirection ability can be done subconsciously through some simple calculations as he was shown doing so as a child 5 years. He just needs to calculate the minimum required forces like gravity, air pressure, light, oxygen, heat, sound wavelength, etc. and redirect everything else. Things such as light, sound, and gravity are calibrated to pass through this field for his convenience, though he can undo this if he chooses to. For defensive use, Karl subconsciously establishes a filter that analyzes everything as harmful or not, and uses his reflect to push away anything that could harm him. Examples of these would be high-velocity vectors that are reflected, such as bullets, which Karl obviously could not consciously react to, as the speed of a bullet is immensely high. He was also able to re-direct nuclear warhead. It is the default and the most basic use of Karl's vectors, allowing him to be protected from nearly any sort of attack, and he even boasts that with it he is able to even withstand a nuclear missile, shock-wave, heat, and radiation. However, after he causes a dust-explosion he mentions that it seems that he might not actually be able to survive it due to being deprived of oxygen in the center of vacuum created by the explosion. Though he quickly counters that it becomes a none issue by simply having an oxygen tank on him about the size of a can of hairspray. It is this barrier that reflects anything harmful to him that gave him his infamous look. His albino appearance is because his body doesn't need to produce protection from the harmful UV rays as Karl's vectors does it for him which has caused his body to stop producing Melanin as it no longer needs to. Moreover, his androgynous appearance is due to his vectors, as there is lack of outside stimulus, there is an imbalance of hormones that gave him his looks. In the past, Karl may have not been able to control the redirection of vectors and may have been the cause of the incident where a group of children gets hurt due to his vectors, leading to Japan to military forces trying to take him down instead of malice in his part. The barrier for his redirection is not an absolute defense. Since it only reverses the vectors that are coming towards him, any vector that comes towards his barrier and pulls away at the exact moment before hitting its field will go towards Karl, which means the most effective method to get through his redirection is Diclonius’s Vectors but only if that Diclonius’s vectors are strong enough to disrupt his redirection filter, rather than immediately bypassing it. Furthermore, attacks that are built upon laws or vectors unknown to him can penetrate his defense. However, due to the nature of his vectors and Karl’s massive calculating prowess, Karl can change the rules of his filter system.

Vector Manipulation: Vector Control  is the active effect of Karl and requires active calculations in order to maintain it, as even a slight error can nullify the effect. A recent discovery of Karl’s due to him not being aware of his own potential, the effect allows Karl to manipulate vectors instead of redirecting them. It is most likely this effect of being able control nearly everything in the world through vectors that Karl’s own potential is described as "The One Who Wields the Power of God", even more so now that he can analyze and understand different physical laws.

APPLICATIONS
Earthquake Generation: By altering the vector of force applied to the ground by his feet, he causes a little explosion made of earth and rocks to attack his opponents. At the beginning of the series this was his most common method of attack. He can also use this to propel himself forward, or cause massive destruction to the ground and surrounding buildings due to shock-waves created by the impact.

Tactile Telekinesis: By touching an object, he can use his ability to change the magnitude of vectors he comes in contact with, such as seen during his fight with Lucy. This allows him to change the vectors of objects in such a way that he can turn them to projectiles. When he lightly kicked a rock to make it shoot like a bullet, or when he stomped on train rails to push them out of their sockets, and lightly knocked on them to make those rails rain upon his target. This ability also allows him to mimic superhuman strength, as he once used it to pick up and throw a concrete wall. By simply pressing his palm against the ground or kicking a stray piece of rubble, Karl can absorb the ambient rotational and kinetic energy of the earth beneath him, funneling it into ordinary pebbles to launch them at hypersonic, artillery-shell velocities or reversing the structural stress vectors within reinforced steel bulkheads to make entire buildings implode inward

Aerokinesis: He can re-vector the surrounding winds and force them to congregate at a single point creating an extremely high velocity wind, but it had flaws like when the wind is moving in an abnormal direction or when his vector calculations are disturbed by sound.

Plasma Generation: He can even create plasma by further compressing the wind at high speeds in a single point.

Ground Manipulation: Karl can manipulate the ground beneath his feet. Besides creating earthquakes and explosions of ground and rock, he can cause objects lodged in the ground or even just placed on the ground to shoot out at incredible speeds in the direction he wants them to. He can also reshape the ground into spear-like pillars to attack the opponent or open ravines in the ground beneath them. In a snowy territory, Karl can create snow tsunamis or even melt snow into water while turning it into a high pressure water cutter.

Acceleration: By controlling the vectors around his body he can achieve inhuman speed.

Kinetic Energy Manipulation: is shown after he uses Vector Control, He takes control of the planet's rotational vectors and transfers an enormous amount of that energy into one devastating attack. This attack used up so much of the planets rotational energy that it slowed down the earth's rotation by about 5 minutes.

Mind Hacking: In accord to him by redirecting the electrical signals of the human body he can take 'control' over them and rewrite the memories and personality of the people. However this type of application is extremely difficult, as the precision of this process requires all his brainpower to a point when he doesn't have enough calculating ability for his redirection leaving him vulnerable. With Karl’s calculation ability reduced to less than half, this application seems to be no longer usable.

Flight: By controlling the wind around him he creates about 4 high-powered tornadoes behind him to allow him to fly. He is also able to redirect the vectors of gravity upon him.

Sound Manipulation: Karl can redirect and even amplify the sound around him. He can even use sound as a sonar to map the surrounding areas.

Sound Nullifying: By tweaking his Redirection to reflect sound.

Bloodflow Control: By touching his opponent he can kill them by either reversing their blood flow or just exploding them. Where he received a cut wound on his arm by Lucy, he was able to survive because he used his ability and brought them through his destroyed veins. Even more horrifyingly, when Karl makes skin-to-skin contact with a living opponent, his micro-vectors bypass armour and muscle entirely to infiltrate their internal physiology, allowing him to effortlessly reverse the directional flow of their blood, lock the bio-electrical currents firing across their central nervous system, or invert the air pressure inside their lungs in a fraction of a second.

Bioelectricity Control: By touching a person, Karl can control a person's bioelectricity and use it to electrocute them. He can also manipulate the electric currents inside their nervous system and use it to make them explode or destroy all of their nerves.

Vector Analysis: Karl can analyze all vectors he comes into contact with. Using this ability he can sense and perceive the environment around him entirely through vectors, obtaining information such as frequency, speed, magnitude, size, structure, temperature, etc. He can use this ability to perceive things out of a normal human's sensory range, such as low-frequency sounds, radiation, and fields when they interact with his redirection. Besides the obvious advantage superhuman senses give, this means he can analyze enemy powers to adapt his redirection in case it doesn't work correctly and even give medical checkups.

Vector Transformation: Karl can amplify and convert existing vectors around him, such as weight, to create an invisible force that he can use to great affect, such as forming a razor-thin blade that he can shoot at a target as a silent and invisible cutting attack or creating a force that absorbs everything in an area towards a designated point, as if mimicking a black hole's gravity.

Lacking Diclonius Virus: Because standard Diclonii transmit the vector virus by physically passing their phantom arms through a human host's body, Karl’s lack of extendable limbs naturally prevents him from infecting others the way Lucy does. Female Diclonii infect humans when their invisible telekinetic hands phase inside a person's flesh to alter their reproductive cells. Since Karl’s vectors form a microscopic, skin-tight redirection field rather than reaching outward, he has no appendages to insert into a host As a true, natural-born male Diclonius, Karl represents a standalone evolutionary branch rather than a "Queen" designed to wipe out humanity through viral propagation. His biology prioritises absolute individual survival over species reproduction. Chief Kakuzawa would view Karl as an irreplaceable genetic anomaly. Unlike Silpelits who only produce sterile offspring via infection, Karl carries pure, natural Diclonius DNA, making him far more valuable alive to Kakuzawa's twisted breeding plans than a standard carrier. Unlike Lucy, who subconsciously infects people even when she doesn't intend to kill them, Karl never has to worry about accidentally turning innocent bystanders into ticking time bombs—his only threat to others is deliberate physical force. He still possesses his natural reproductive organs to reproduce then spread the virus through contact, which he has no interest in doing so.

WEAKNESSES
Mental Bandwidth & Calculation Overload. Karl’s barrier does not work by magic; his brain must actively distinguish between harmless ambient forces (gravity, breathable air, visible light) and lethal attacks. If he is overwhelmed by extreme sensory chaos or forced to calculate too many complex variables at once, his reflection filter can lag for a fraction of a second.

Vector-Inversion Exploits. An enemy who understands the exact mechanics of Karl’s reflection can pull back a punch or reverse the direction of a kinetic strike at the exact microsecond of impact. Because Karl’s passive barrier automatically inverts incoming vectors, reversing an attack right as it touches his skin causes his own shield to pull the blow inward instead of pushing it away.

Environmental & Indirect Traps. Karl’s vectors only govern forces that directly touch his skin or an object he is physically holding. He is still a biological organism who needs oxygen to breathe; trapping him in a sealed vacuum, flooding a room with heavy non-toxic gases that displace oxygen, or starving him of food and water will bypass his defence completely if he doesn’t escape that predicament.

Severe Sensory Sensitivity. Spending fifteen years in a silent, pitch-black vault left Karl’s eyes and ears hyper-sensitive. Sudden, blinding flashbangs, high-decibel acoustic weapons, or chaotic urban crowds can trigger debilitating migraines that disrupt his focus and temporarily drop his barrier.

Protectiveness Over Innocent Children. Karl’s greatest tactical weakness is his soft spot for abused Silpelits like Nana or Mariko. To shield a child standing behind him, he has to consciously widen his vector calculations to cover them too, leaving him open to coordinated flank attacks while his focus is divided.

Self-Loathing & Restraint. Despite his loud, arrogant threats, Karl secretly hates killing and subconsciously holds back against ordinary, powerless humans. A ruthless opponent willing to exploit his reluctance to slaughter innocent bystanders can force him onto the defensive.
